WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.163 --> 00:00:08.781
<i>Morley: I'm not wrong about Flint.</i>

2
00:00:08.832 --> 00:00:11.483
<i>- To him we're all disposable.
- I don't believe that.</i>

3
00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:14.870
That's because you don't
know about Mrs. Barlow.

4
00:00:14.955 --> 00:00:16.171
You found the schedule.

5
00:00:16.256 --> 00:00:18.507
What if I forgo payment for the schedule

6
00:00:18.591 --> 00:00:20.542
in exchange for my share of the prize?

7
00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:21.961
We'll need some additional items.

8
00:00:22.012 --> 00:00:24.380
<i>- New guns... 12-pounders.
- You'll have it.</i>

9
00:00:24.464 --> 00:00:25.848
Without the Urca we have nothing.

10
00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:28.000
Without Vane we don't have the Urca.

11
00:00:28.051 --> 00:00:30.853
Our friend tried to protect
you. You left anyway.

12
00:00:30.937 --> 00:00:34.506
- Why?
- How did you feel when she threw you aside?

13
00:00:34.557 --> 00:00:36.692
<i>- (Max screaming)
- Eleanor. wait.</i>

14
00:00:36.776 --> 00:00:38.844
(grunting)

15
00:00:38.895 --> 00:00:41.363
<i>Eleanor: Listen to me
carefully. You are finished.</i>

16
00:00:41.448 --> 00:00:44.233
Unless you decide to join
the crew of Captain Flint.

17
00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:45.684
Looks like she just gave us a ship.

18
00:00:45.735 --> 00:00:47.820
Ship with no captain.

19
00:00:47.871 --> 00:00:50.122
- So sorry he did this to you.
- He didn't do this to me.

20
00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:51.657
You did.

21
00:00:54.694 --> 00:00:56.795
<i>(theme music playing)</i>

22
00:00:56.796 --> 00:00:59.796
- synced and corrected by chamallow -
- www.addic7ed.com -

23
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:07.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

24
00:02:31.931 --> 00:02:34.283
<i>(bell rings)</i>

25
00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.211
Captain Gates.

26
00:02:48.414 --> 00:02:50.299
(knocks)

27
00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.802
It's time.

28
00:03:01.794 --> 00:03:03.595
(crew murmuring)

29
00:03:13.606 --> 00:03:16.825
First item for the council
concerns leadership.

30
00:03:16.909 --> 00:03:19.528
As you know. I've been
asked to serve as captain

31
00:03:19.612 --> 00:03:22.281
of the Ranger when next we sail.

32
00:03:22.332 --> 00:03:24.649
Obviously that means less
time spent with you idiots.

33
00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.318
- (crew laughs)
- So...

34
00:03:26.369 --> 00:03:29.988
you will need somebody to act as
your quartermaster in the meantime.

35
00:03:30.039 --> 00:03:33.491
Unless anybody's got any better ideas.

36
00:03:33.543 --> 00:03:35.660
I was thinking Billy Bones.

37
00:03:35.712 --> 00:03:37.629
(cheering)

38
00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.018
I thought so.

39
00:03:43.102 --> 00:03:44.803
Billy.

40
00:03:47.023 --> 00:03:48.724
<i>Billy: Ahem.</i>

41
00:03:48.808 --> 00:03:52.177
Next item... careening.

42
00:03:52.228 --> 00:03:54.396
<i>- (grumbling)
- Man: Bad start. Billy.</i>

43
00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.115
She's long overdue. If
we're gonna win the Urca.

44
00:03:57.183 --> 00:03:58.984
the Walrus must be shipshape.
That means we tip her.

45
00:03:59.035 --> 00:04:01.153
Plain and simple. The question is.

46
00:04:01.204 --> 00:04:02.871
where do we do the tipping?

47
00:04:02.955 --> 00:04:05.957
- Wherever there's plenty of rum.
- (Laughing)

48
00:04:06.025 --> 00:04:07.826
As always. the ship's account is open.

49
00:04:07.877 --> 00:04:11.213
Rum casks and Mr. Simpson's
buttered oranges are on their way.

50
00:04:11.297 --> 00:04:13.749
And the pigs are being
readied for Mr. Silver's spit.

51
00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:17.369
Now. to return to the issue of location.

52
00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.804
What about the fuck tent?

53
00:04:18.871 --> 00:04:21.506
That's probably something we can discuss.

54
00:04:21.557 --> 00:04:24.760
(crew chanting) Fuck tent! Fuck tent!

55
00:04:26.212 --> 00:04:27.429
Mr. De Groot.

56
00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.384
You may not like what I have to say.

57
00:04:32.435 --> 00:04:35.354
<i>but if it remains unsaid. I fear the worst.</i>

58
00:04:35.405 --> 00:04:37.555
<i>I've inspected the shoreline
proposed by the captain</i>

59
00:04:37.607 --> 00:04:40.108
for this undertaking and
it is simply unsuitable

60
00:04:40.193 --> 00:04:42.577
to the task at hand. The anchorage is poor.

61
00:04:42.662 --> 00:04:44.562
<i>The incline too steep.</i>

62
00:04:44.614 --> 00:04:47.232
I cannot endorse it. The
risk for calamity is too high.

63
00:04:47.283 --> 00:04:50.252
<i>With the crew's assent.</i>

64
00:04:50.336 --> 00:04:53.905
I ask for time to find
a more suitable beach.

65
00:04:53.956 --> 00:04:55.340
<i>Flint: And delay our efforts by how long?</i>

66
00:04:55.408 --> 00:04:58.460
Two weeks? A month?

67
00:05:01.631 --> 00:05:03.515
A clean hull

68
00:05:03.582 --> 00:05:06.768
means an extra knot or two in speed.

69
00:05:06.853 --> 00:05:09.754
five degrees or more in coming about.

70
00:05:09.806 --> 00:05:12.524
It's essential to the job at hand.

71
00:05:13.926 --> 00:05:17.062
If we had weeks. we'd surely take them.

72
00:05:17.113 --> 00:05:19.597
But we must sail within days

73
00:05:19.649 --> 00:05:21.599
<i>if we are to meet the Urca.</i>

74
00:05:21.651 --> 00:05:24.069
Now. Mr. De Groot's concerns are valid...

75
00:05:25.738 --> 00:05:28.156
<i>but they come at a price.</i>

76
00:05:28.241 --> 00:05:32.627
$5 million in Spanish gold. to be exact.

77
00:05:32.712 --> 00:05:35.914
(crew murmuring)

78
00:05:43.339 --> 00:05:45.290
All those in favor of the captain's plan

79
00:05:45.341 --> 00:05:46.558
to careen here near the bay?

80
00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:49.144
All: Aye!

81
00:05:49.228 --> 00:05:51.146
It would appear the ayes have it.

82
00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:52.764
Nay.

83
00:05:57.636 --> 00:06:00.989
Mr. Morley's dissent is noted
along with Mr. De Groot's.

84
00:06:03.693 --> 00:06:05.527
All right. let's beach this bitch.

85
00:06:05.611 --> 00:06:09.281
Yeah. quick question. then. Where
are we on the issue of the fuck tent?

86
00:06:09.332 --> 00:06:12.584
- Crew: Yeah!
- This job is gonna happen fast.

87
00:06:12.651 --> 00:06:16.087
That means more risk. more danger.

88
00:06:16.155 --> 00:06:17.839
Now you've put a great deal of trust in me

89
00:06:17.924 --> 00:06:20.125
to serve in Mr. Gates' absence.
and I take that seriously.

90
00:06:20.176 --> 00:06:23.712
So given the potential
for distraction and delay

91
00:06:23.796 --> 00:06:25.514
at a time that we need to be at our best.

92
00:06:25.598 --> 00:06:28.300
perhaps we can all agree to forgo.

93
00:06:28.351 --> 00:06:31.887
just this once. a fuck tent.

94
00:06:36.976 --> 00:06:38.977
<i>(thumping)</i>

95
00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.962
(flies buzzing)

96
00:06:57.029 --> 00:06:59.080
You shouldn't have.

97
00:07:06.172 --> 00:07:08.173
(men shouting)

98
00:07:14.263 --> 00:07:16.932
Stale winds. still waters.

99
00:07:17.016 --> 00:07:19.651
Don't be such an old lady.

100
00:07:19.718 --> 00:07:21.069
The men will rise to it.

101
00:07:21.153 --> 00:07:23.721
What say you. Mr. Quartermaster?

102
00:07:23.773 --> 00:07:25.890
You think it's a good idea?

103
00:07:25.942 --> 00:07:28.109
Yeah. I think the captain
knows what he's doing.

104
00:07:31.664 --> 00:07:32.914
<i>(bell rings)</i>

105
00:07:32.999 --> 00:07:36.535
That's because you don't
know about Mrs. Barlow.

106
00:07:37.837 --> 00:07:39.955
Who's Mrs. Barlow?

107
00:07:43.543 --> 00:07:45.410
Number of years back.

108
00:07:45.461 --> 00:07:48.380
before you crewed up with us.

109
00:07:48.431 --> 00:07:51.883
Flint had us hunting a merchant ship.

110
00:07:51.934 --> 00:07:54.252
the Maria Aleyne.

111
00:07:54.303 --> 00:07:55.920
Sephardic trade...

112
00:07:55.972 --> 00:07:59.357
gold. pearls. jewels.

113
00:07:59.425 --> 00:08:03.061
"More than we'd ever know
what to do with." he said.

114
00:08:03.112 --> 00:08:05.814
But that's Flint's gift. isn't it?

115
00:08:05.898 --> 00:08:10.151
Always knows just what
to say to push us harder.

116
00:08:10.236 --> 00:08:13.955
further. make us all pull
together for the cause.

117
00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:16.541
We tracked that bitch for months

118
00:08:16.609 --> 00:08:19.077
without refitting or careening.

119
00:08:19.128 --> 00:08:21.830
till finally we spotted her.

120
00:08:21.914 --> 00:08:24.799
We lost good men taking her

121
00:08:24.884 --> 00:08:28.503
for a haul nowhere near
what Flint had promised.

122
00:08:28.588 --> 00:08:31.956
While I was exploring the hold.

123
00:08:32.008 --> 00:08:35.260
I chanced upon a cabin
and that's when I heard it.

124
00:08:35.311 --> 00:08:39.514
'Twas a man and a woman
begging for their lives.

125
00:08:40.766 --> 00:08:44.352
"Spare us. and our fortune's yours."

126
00:08:44.437 --> 00:08:48.490
For a moment. I thought all our shares

127
00:08:48.574 --> 00:08:50.825
were gonna be worth a whole lot more.

128
00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:54.663
But that's when the screams began.

129
00:08:57.533 --> 00:09:01.119
And when I watched the murderer leave.

130
00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:03.755
I saw him plain.

131
00:09:07.826 --> 00:09:09.260
Did you tell anyone?

132
00:09:09.328 --> 00:09:11.296
Gates.

133
00:09:12.548 --> 00:09:16.434
He was unmoved. to say the least.

134
00:09:16.502 --> 00:09:20.805
"Just one rich bastard
less in the world." he said.

135
00:09:20.856 --> 00:09:23.858
At the time. I'll admit. I took his point.

136
00:09:25.444 --> 00:09:28.229
But days later we come ashore.

137
00:09:28.314 --> 00:09:31.733
I see a lady waiting for Flint.

138
00:09:31.817 --> 00:09:35.787
The rest of the crew thought she's
just some fancy bit of Puritan tail.

139
00:09:35.854 --> 00:09:38.206
But when Flint reaches her.

140
00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:41.826
<i>two words escape his lips.</i>

141
00:09:41.877 --> 00:09:43.578
<i>"They're dead."</i>

142
00:09:43.663 --> 00:09:46.214
Hunting the Maria Aleyne

143
00:09:46.298 --> 00:09:48.800
was never about money.

144
00:09:48.867 --> 00:09:50.669
It was an execution.

145
00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:53.254
<i>All those men we lost taking her.</i>

146
00:09:53.339 --> 00:09:56.207
they died so Flint could settle

147
00:09:56.258 --> 00:10:00.044
<i>some personal vendetta for her.</i>

148
00:10:00.096 --> 00:10:02.931
You watch.

149
00:10:03.015 --> 00:10:06.735
Good men will die for some hidden agenda.

150
00:10:06.819 --> 00:10:08.987
The Barlow woman's agenda.

151
00:10:09.054 --> 00:10:10.739
Mark my words. Billy.

152
00:10:12.891 --> 00:10:15.076
It's all happening again.

153
00:10:19.632 --> 00:10:22.100
<i>(thumping)</i>

154
00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:33.261
(moaning)

155
00:10:33.345 --> 00:10:36.181
<i>(thumping. moaning continues)</i>

156
00:10:39.885 --> 00:10:42.053
(gasps)

157
00:10:53.199 --> 00:10:55.450
(sighs)

158
00:11:09.465 --> 00:11:12.000
<i>Miranda: Will you be staying long?</i>

159
00:11:13.469 --> 00:11:15.420
I have to get back.

160
00:11:20.309 --> 00:11:22.927
If you're upset with me.
I'd appreciate you saying so.

161
00:11:25.798 --> 00:11:27.432
You know why I'm upset.

162
00:11:28.934 --> 00:11:30.301
Because I read to him?

163
00:11:30.352 --> 00:11:32.470
There's a whole shelf full of books.

164
00:11:32.521 --> 00:11:34.972
Why'd you have to read him that one?

165
00:11:35.024 --> 00:11:38.109
Perhaps because I am no longer willing

166
00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:41.329
to bury it on a shelf and
pretend it has no meaning for me.

167
00:11:46.335 --> 00:11:50.338
That book is something
I shared with Thomas.

168
00:11:54.593 --> 00:11:56.878
<i>I just missed it.</i>

169
00:11:58.497 --> 00:12:00.832
Our life then

170
00:12:00.883 --> 00:12:03.468
when he was alive.

171
00:12:05.938 --> 00:12:07.639
I can feel myself forgetting it

172
00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:09.057
and I don't want to forget it.

173
00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:15.363
This place. this life that
we've been living here.

174
00:12:15.447 --> 00:12:18.650
it doesn't feel like living anymore.

175
00:12:21.821 --> 00:12:24.489
I can't be alone in feeling this way.

176
00:12:26.959 --> 00:12:29.460
Some part of you must feel it. too.

177
00:12:45.427 --> 00:12:47.729
Things will get better here.

178
00:12:49.682 --> 00:12:51.900
I promise you they will.

179
00:13:03.996 --> 00:13:05.780
Here you go.

180
00:13:14.406 --> 00:13:16.174
Christ.

181
00:13:16.241 --> 00:13:19.460
<i>One week without a ship and
you go completely to hell.</i>

182
00:13:19.545 --> 00:13:21.763
Is it too much to ask
that you not pick a fight

183
00:13:21.847 --> 00:13:24.349
over every insult thrown our way?

184
00:13:24.416 --> 00:13:27.101
<i>Especially when I'm out there
swallowing what little pride I have left</i>

185
00:13:27.186 --> 00:13:28.887
trying to set things right.

186
00:13:31.423 --> 00:13:33.691
I see we've graduated to opium.

187
00:13:39.064 --> 00:13:42.116
Miss Guthrie has dealt us quite a blow.

188
00:13:42.201 --> 00:13:44.652
But we still have assets.

189
00:13:44.737 --> 00:13:47.956
<i>Eight loyal men. my wits.</i>

190
00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:50.441
<i>and an unshakable captain.</i>

191
00:13:50.492 --> 00:13:52.076
(sniffs)

192
00:13:52.127 --> 00:13:54.412
I'm doing what I can to
regain us our livelihood.

193
00:13:54.463 --> 00:13:56.915
but once that's done.
this crew. such as it is.

194
00:13:56.966 --> 00:13:59.584
will need its captain back.

195
00:13:59.635 --> 00:14:01.502
See what you can do about finding him.

196
00:14:08.394 --> 00:14:10.345
Fuck you. Jack.

197
00:14:40.542 --> 00:14:42.593
It was an isolated incident.

198
00:14:42.661 --> 00:14:45.263
No cause for concern.

199
00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:48.499
Your girl humiliated one of
this island's strongest earners.

200
00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:50.301
threatened his crew with embargoes

201
00:14:50.352 --> 00:14:53.021
so they had no choice
but to toss him aside.

202
00:14:53.105 --> 00:14:54.689
I've had three other captains approach me

203
00:14:54.773 --> 00:14:56.441
all asking the same question...

204
00:14:56.508 --> 00:14:58.609
who's next to lose their livelihood

205
00:14:58.677 --> 00:15:00.611
<i>because they crossed her on the wrong day?</i>

206
00:15:00.679 --> 00:15:02.196
No one is next.

207
00:15:03.732 --> 00:15:06.567
Every morning for months now
when I walk the beach into town.

208
00:15:06.652 --> 00:15:09.704
I see Captain Lilywhite
standing on his stoop

209
00:15:09.788 --> 00:15:11.689
and jabbering away to
anyone who will listen

210
00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:14.409
<i>about the evils of a centralized fence.</i>

211
00:15:14.493 --> 00:15:16.828
Arguing that this island will never be free

212
00:15:16.879 --> 00:15:20.331
until we all come together to
cast off the tyrannical yoke

213
00:15:20.382 --> 00:15:23.084
of Queen Eleanor.

214
00:15:23.168 --> 00:15:25.253
I see him out there. too.

215
00:15:26.588 --> 00:15:28.539
And I have never seen
any more than three men

216
00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:30.207
paying him any attention.

217
00:15:30.259 --> 00:15:31.426
Half-wits. all of them.

218
00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:33.428
There were 12 of them this morning.

219
00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:37.815
This business with Vane has changed things.

220
00:15:38.934 --> 00:15:41.519
Get control of her. Mr. Scott.

221
00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:43.154
before it's too late.

222
00:15:46.191 --> 00:15:49.410
Sail spotted. The Andromache.

223
00:15:53.398 --> 00:15:55.500
<i>(door closes)</i>

224
00:15:57.336 --> 00:15:59.287
Captain Bryson is
arriving on the Andromache.

225
00:15:59.371 --> 00:16:00.738
<i>You'd best get down to the beach.</i>

226
00:16:00.789 --> 00:16:02.256
What did Captain Hornigold want?

227
00:16:05.377 --> 00:16:08.212
Let me guess.

228
00:16:08.263 --> 00:16:09.797
The captains grousing about last week

229
00:16:09.882 --> 00:16:11.132
think I've lost my grip on reason.

230
00:16:11.216 --> 00:16:13.518
<i>Fuck Hornigold.</i>

231
00:16:13.585 --> 00:16:15.269
Fuck the captains and fuck anyone else

232
00:16:15.354 --> 00:16:17.355
who doesn't like the
way I manage this place.

233
00:16:23.929 --> 00:16:26.814
What we're about to
attempt with Captain Bryson.

234
00:16:26.899 --> 00:16:29.117
it is very risky.

235
00:16:29.201 --> 00:16:30.985
If he will not cooperate.

236
00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.071
we cannot. under any circumstances.

237
00:16:33.122 --> 00:16:35.123
attempt to detain him.

238
00:16:35.207 --> 00:16:36.824
- What makes you think I'd try?
- 'Cause I know you.

239
00:16:36.909 --> 00:16:38.709
I know what you think is at stake.

240
00:16:38.777 --> 00:16:41.329
And I know you think you
cannot take no for an answer.

241
00:16:41.413 --> 00:16:43.164
Why should I?

242
00:16:45.717 --> 00:16:48.252
Eleanor. if you make a move

243
00:16:48.303 --> 00:16:50.088
against Captain Bryson or his ship.

244
00:16:50.139 --> 00:16:52.723
you'll be making a move against
the Guthrie Trading Company.

245
00:16:52.791 --> 00:16:54.675
A direct affront to your grandfather

246
00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:56.477
<i>and his interests in Boston.</i>

247
00:16:56.562 --> 00:16:58.629
That ship belongs to him.

248
00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.231
When he finds out what you've done.

249
00:17:00.298 --> 00:17:03.684
no one... not I nor your father...

250
00:17:03.769 --> 00:17:07.271
will able to protect you
from the consequences.

251
00:17:07.322 --> 00:17:11.075
If Bryson balks. we must let him go.

252
00:17:11.143 --> 00:17:15.029
And the guns Flint needs? What about them?

253
00:17:15.114 --> 00:17:16.781
We'll find them some other way.

254
00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.317
I never ask anything of you.

255
00:17:20.369 --> 00:17:22.086
This I must insist on.

256
