441
00:29:24.475 --> 00:29:27.227
- I can't do it. Jack.
- Of course you can.

442
00:29:27.312 --> 00:29:30.213
You simply present my crew's haul to
Miss Guthrie as if it were your own.

443
00:29:30.265 --> 00:29:32.099
You get a percentage. Everybody wins.

444
00:29:32.183 --> 00:29:34.017
I get caught selling a
grain of salt for you.

445
00:29:34.068 --> 00:29:36.570
the girl puts my crew
on the outs same as you.

446
00:29:36.654 --> 00:29:39.740
<i>I just can't risk it.</i>

447
00:29:39.824 --> 00:29:42.075
It ain't you she has a problem with. Jack.

448
00:29:42.160 --> 00:29:44.027
Why stick with him?

449
00:29:45.246 --> 00:29:47.114
<i>Anne: It's a good question.</i>

450
00:29:47.198 --> 00:29:48.949
No. it's not.

451
00:29:49.033 --> 00:29:50.567
There are other ships.

452
00:29:50.618 --> 00:29:52.569
Had a few offers. have you?

453
00:29:52.620 --> 00:29:55.122
Makes sense. You'd be an asset to any crew.

454
00:29:55.206 --> 00:29:57.958
Now ask how many offers
good old Jack has received

455
00:29:58.042 --> 00:30:00.294
since our run-in with the lady Guthrie.

456
00:30:00.378 --> 00:30:02.379
