currently docked at Harbour Island.

509
00:32:53.768 --> 00:32:55.852
Docked outside your home.

510
00:32:55.920 --> 00:33:00.107
<i>My intent was to stop there first
and unload the slaves in my hold.</i>

511
00:33:00.191 --> 00:33:01.758
<i>but when I saw her. I thought better of it.</i>

512
00:33:01.809 --> 00:33:05.946
His Majesty's ships often
use my port for resupply.

513
00:33:06.030 --> 00:33:09.066
What are you implying?

514
00:33:12.937 --> 00:33:14.871
I'd like to speak with your father alone.

515
00:33:17.458 --> 00:33:19.409
Whatever you can say to
him. you can say to me.

516
00:33:19.460 --> 00:33:22.079
Eleanor. it's all right.

517
00:33:33.341 --> 00:33:35.642
<i>(door opens)</i>

518
00:33:37.962 --> 00:33:39.679
<i>(door closes)</i>

519
00:33:43.267 --> 00:33:45.152
Your father can handle this.

520
00:33:45.236 --> 00:33:46.937
He'll get you those guns.

521
00:33:46.988 --> 00:33:48.939
Perhaps.

522
00:34:01.586 --> 00:34:03.170
I couldn't leave it to chance.

523
00:34:05.423 --> 00:34:08.458
Let us be frank.

524
00:34:08.509 --> 00:34:10.260
You and I both know the low regard

525
00:34:10.327 --> 00:34:12.045
in which your family in Boston holds you.

526
00:34:12.130 --> 00:34:15.182
Quite frank. it seems.

527
00:34:15.266 --> 00:34:17.684
If I returned unarmed and they find

528
00:34:17.768 --> 00:34:19.603
that I did so under these circumstances

529
00:34:19.670 --> 00:34:22.556
with only your orders as justification.

530
00:34:22.640 --> 00:34:26.193
I'll be buried in a shallow
grave somewhere out in Cambridge.

531
00:34:26.277 --> 00:34:29.512
And what exactly do you believe
"these circumstances" to be?

532
00:34:29.564 --> 00:34:32.115
The Navy on your doorstep.

533
00:34:32.183 --> 00:34:34.034
You and your daughter

534
00:34:34.118 --> 00:34:37.070
supporting a plan as reckless as this.

535
00:34:37.155 --> 00:34:40.407
It would seem. sir. that something's gone
terribly wrong with the operation here

536
00:34:40.491 --> 00:34:43.660
and you two are scrambling
to save yourselves.

537
00:34:45.496 --> 00:34:47.797
Tell me I'm wrong.

538
00:34:49.867 --> 00:34:53.386
Let me tell you how wrong you are.

539
00:34:53.471 --> 00:34:55.589
I knew you wouldn't approve.

540
00:34:55.673 --> 00:34:58.341
But I couldn't let him leave
here without giving up those guns.

541
00:34:58.392 --> 00:35:00.010
I'm sorry.

542
00:35:00.061 --> 00:35:01.811
With everything we've been through.

543
00:35:01.879 --> 00:35:03.880
with everything I've done for you...

544
00:35:03.931 --> 00:35:06.183
- I'm doing this for us both.
- You lied.

545
00:35:10.354 --> 00:35:11.738
Shame on you.

546
00:35:34.795 --> 00:35:36.429
The guns are yours.

547
00:35:37.765 --> 00:35:39.099
Mr. Hayes.

548
00:35:50.761 --> 00:35:53.146
Richard: Truly something
to behold. this place.

549
00:35:53.231 --> 00:35:54.898
You should be proud.

550
00:35:56.901 --> 00:35:59.069
Come now. Mr. Scott.

551
00:35:59.120 --> 00:36:02.122
It's as much your work as Eleanor's.

552
00:36:02.206 --> 00:36:05.742
What is this if not the
moment of your vindication?

553
00:36:07.411 --> 00:36:08.795
It's time we got you back.

554
00:36:08.879 --> 00:36:10.914
She'll get herself killed.

555
00:36:15.386 --> 00:36:18.638
If she proceeds with this
Spanish galleon business.

556
00:36:18.723 --> 00:36:20.640
attempting to steal
treasure from one empire

557
00:36:20.725 --> 00:36:22.292
to finance a war against another.

558
00:36:22.343 --> 00:36:24.177
she will get herself killed.

559
00:36:24.262 --> 00:36:27.130
Whether by English noose or Spanish sword.

560
00:36:27.181 --> 00:36:29.432
it's inevitable and you know it.

561
00:36:30.935 --> 00:36:32.936
If she proceeds...

562
00:36:34.655 --> 00:36:36.573
what did you say to Bryson in that room?

563
00:36:37.775 --> 00:36:39.993
Rest assured I had a plan.

564
00:36:40.077 --> 00:36:42.195
Not just to end this insanity.

565
00:36:42.280 --> 00:36:44.981
but to contend with what comes next.

566
00:36:45.032 --> 00:36:47.534
To keep her safe.

567
00:36:47.618 --> 00:36:49.502
I don't envy you.

568
00:36:49.587 --> 00:36:53.673
You know that she'll stop at
nothing to save this place.

569
00:36:53.758 --> 00:36:55.458
A place where she matters.

570
00:36:55.509 --> 00:36:57.994
<i>A place where you matter.</i>

571
00:36:58.045 --> 00:37:01.047
Except that in your
heart you know the truth.

572
00:37:03.267 --> 00:37:06.553
Places like this aren't meant to last.

573
00:37:08.172 --> 00:37:10.390
Help me. Mr. Scott.

574
00:37:11.976 --> 00:37:13.443
Please.

575
00:37:13.510 --> 00:37:16.313
Help me save her from herself.

576
00:37:30.578 --> 00:37:32.495
<i>(branch snaps)</i>

577
00:37:37.218 --> 00:37:39.336
Well. hello.

578
00:37:42.089 --> 00:37:44.057
There's no need to be afraid.

579
00:37:46.761 --> 00:37:49.179
You could help me if you like.

580
00:37:52.767 --> 00:37:54.351
Aren't you the Gladwin boy?

581
00:37:57.321 --> 00:37:59.939
Does your father know
you're out here all alone?

582
00:38:00.024 --> 00:38:01.691
I can take you to him.

583
00:38:04.061 --> 00:38:05.662
Oh!

584
00:38:05.729 --> 00:38:07.997
Witch!

585
00:38:27.017 --> 00:38:28.885
(grunting)

586
00:38:31.889 --> 00:38:33.056
(meows)

587
00:38:33.107 --> 00:38:36.142
Captain. Visitor.

588
00:38:42.783 --> 00:38:45.601
The guns are yours.

589
00:38:45.653 --> 00:38:47.821
Captain Bryson's preparing
to off-load them as we speak.

590
00:38:47.905 --> 00:38:51.107
Mr. O'Malley is on the
lookout to ensure he complies.

591
00:38:51.158 --> 00:38:53.209
Take a seat.

592
00:39:01.719 --> 00:39:03.503
To our endeavor

593
00:39:03.587 --> 00:39:06.589
and success close at hand.

594
00:39:10.428 --> 00:39:11.728
What's wrong?

595
00:39:11.795 --> 00:39:13.847
Your father step out of line?

596
00:39:13.931 --> 00:39:15.982
It's Mr. Scott.

597
00:39:16.066 --> 00:39:19.185
In order to guarantee
Captain Bryson's acquiescence.

598
00:39:19.270 --> 00:39:21.771
I put a plan into place
without Mr. Scott's knowledge.

599
00:39:23.640 --> 00:39:25.658
I lied to him.

600
00:39:25.743 --> 00:39:27.527
<i>Betrayed his trust.</i>

601
00:39:27.611 --> 00:39:30.029
I didn't want to. but I just
didn't think he would understand.

602
00:39:30.114 --> 00:39:32.031
Well. you can't expect him to.

603
00:39:32.116 --> 00:39:34.834
Nobody will believe it's
possible until we show them.

604
00:39:34.919 --> 00:39:36.986
But when that day comes.

605
00:39:37.037 --> 00:39:40.006
you know what they'll say?

606
00:39:40.090 --> 00:39:42.959
They'll say that it was inevitable.

607
00:39:46.347 --> 00:39:49.132
<i>(wind rustling)</i>

608
00:39:55.222 --> 00:39:57.807
(creaking)

609
00:39:57.858 --> 00:39:59.859
(cracking)

610
00:40:02.396 --> 00:40:04.147
(timbers groaning)

611
00:40:05.649 --> 00:40:08.201
<i>Man: Get back!</i>

612
00:40:08.285 --> 00:40:09.702
<i>(men shouting)</i>

613
00:40:09.787 --> 00:40:11.621
Back off! Back off!

614
00:40:17.127 --> 00:40:20.029
Get away! Get away!

615
00:40:20.080 --> 00:40:22.632
Everyone. get up to the beach now! Come on!

616
00:40:24.218 --> 00:40:26.469
<i>(ship groaning)</i>

617
00:40:31.208 --> 00:40:33.009
<i>Billy: Let's go! Let's go! Let's go!</i>

618
00:40:33.060 --> 00:40:35.345
<i>(cat meows)</i>

619
00:40:40.050 --> 00:40:41.734
<i>She's going!</i>

620
00:40:44.221 --> 00:40:45.488
Get out!

621
00:41:00.571 --> 00:41:02.922
<i>(Randall screams)</i>

622
00:41:03.007 --> 00:41:05.124
Oh. shit.

623
00:41:05.209 --> 00:41:06.793
Randall!

624
00:41:08.762 --> 00:41:11.214
- I'll go.
- Captain. there's no time.

625
00:41:11.265 --> 00:41:13.049
The mainmast is holding too much weight.

626
00:41:13.100 --> 00:41:14.467
We have to cut her loose!

627
00:41:14.552 --> 00:41:16.352
Save the mast. Don't wait for me.

628
00:41:18.922 --> 00:41:21.107
<i>(Randall screaming)</i>

629
00:41:23.310 --> 00:41:26.429
He's dug in. Help me.

630
00:41:26.480 --> 00:41:29.949
- (meows)
- Me leg! Me leg!

631
00:41:34.371 --> 00:41:37.073
Pull! Pull! One. two. three. pull!

632
00:41:37.124 --> 00:41:39.275
(screaming)

633
00:41:39.326 --> 00:41:41.544
It's taking too long.

634
00:41:46.250 --> 00:41:48.585
How much time do we have?

635
00:41:48.636 --> 00:41:49.752
We don't.

636
00:41:51.755 --> 00:41:53.556
Billy. the time is now!

637
00:41:53.624 --> 00:41:57.260
(wood cracking)

638
00:41:57.311 --> 00:41:59.095
(screaming)

639
00:42:00.598 --> 00:42:02.432
It's no bloody use.

640
00:42:10.474 --> 00:42:13.643
Your belt. Give me your belt.

641
00:42:13.694 --> 00:42:15.111
<i>(ship groaning)</i>

642
00:42:17.164 --> 00:42:18.648
<i>- Billy.
- Man: Cut the ropes!</i>

643
00:42:18.699 --> 00:42:20.833
- Billy!
- All right!

644
00:42:20.918 --> 00:42:23.119
Right.

645
00:42:24.538 --> 00:42:25.622
Do it!

646
00:42:25.673 --> 00:42:27.674
(muffled screaming)

647
00:42:31.595 --> 00:42:34.597
Bite. Bite down on it.

648
00:42:37.351 --> 00:42:39.185
Hold on. Randall.

649
00:42:39.269 --> 00:42:40.353
Hold on.

650
00:42:42.356 --> 00:42:44.774
All right. pull!

651
00:42:49.179 --> 00:42:50.897
(screaming)

652
00:42:55.402 --> 00:42:57.620
<i>(creaking stops)</i>

653
00:43:24.932 --> 00:43:26.933
(sighs)

654
00:43:48.005 --> 00:43:49.872
Shit.

655
00:44:06.273 --> 00:44:08.775
I talked to De Groot. You
did everything you could.

656
00:44:10.561 --> 00:44:13.730
Not everything.

657
00:44:13.781 --> 00:44:15.148
<i>I should have stopped Flint.</i>

658
00:44:15.232 --> 00:44:17.600
Honestly. son.

659
00:44:17.651 --> 00:44:19.569
how could you have done that?

660
00:44:22.456 --> 00:44:24.407
Careful. Billy.

661
00:44:28.829 --> 00:44:31.881
Flint pushed it through and I
went along when I knew better.

662
00:44:31.948 --> 00:44:34.000
Because you know what's at stake here.

663
00:44:34.084 --> 00:44:35.918
You know he's right.

664
00:44:35.969 --> 00:44:37.837
That's not why I...

665
00:44:44.428 --> 00:44:46.596
It's because I'm afraid of him.

666
00:45:15.325 --> 00:45:17.960
Billy and Morley.

667
00:45:18.011 --> 00:45:20.096
That night on the ship.

668
00:45:20.163 --> 00:45:22.048
what were they talking about?

669
00:45:24.000 --> 00:45:25.334
Well. I didn't hear much.

670
00:45:25.385 --> 00:45:28.271
but it sounded like they
were talking about a woman.

671
00:45:28.338 --> 00:45:30.606
Somebody Barlow.

672
00:45:46.790 --> 00:45:48.825
<i>(harpsichord music playing)</i>

673
00:46:04.341 --> 00:46:06.642
<i>(door opens)</i>

674
00:46:21.942 --> 00:46:23.359
Success?

675
00:46:25.362 --> 00:46:27.163
Would you mind?

676
00:46:34.955 --> 00:46:37.540
The music you were playing.

677
00:46:37.591 --> 00:46:41.010
<i>that's Purcell's Chaconne
if I'm not mistaken.</i>

678
00:46:44.882 --> 00:46:46.215
You have an educated ear.

679
00:46:47.584 --> 00:46:50.386
My father employed a
tutor for all his children

680
00:46:50.437 --> 00:46:52.688
so that they might learn
to appreciate music.

681
00:46:52.756 --> 00:46:55.942
I took to it the least of my siblings.

682
00:46:56.026 --> 00:46:59.395
But for reasons beyond
me. some of it stuck.

683
00:47:03.934 --> 00:47:06.736
<i>There's a pronounced sense of sadness</i>

684
00:47:06.787 --> 00:47:08.938
<i>in Purcell's pieces.</i>

685
00:47:08.989 --> 00:47:11.607
Considering your circumstances.

686
00:47:11.658 --> 00:47:13.242
I can understand their appeal.

687
00:47:15.045 --> 00:47:18.297
And what is it you think you
understand of my circumstances?

688
00:47:18.382 --> 00:47:20.216
Truthfully.

689
00:47:20.283 --> 00:47:23.085
I might know everything. Mrs. Hamilton.

690
00:47:25.389 --> 00:47:27.223
<i>Don't be alarmed.</i>

691
00:47:27.290 --> 00:47:30.643
<i>I have no intention of disclosing
your identity to anyone.</i>

692
00:47:30.727 --> 00:47:34.563
I'm sorry. sir. I think you have
me mistaken for someone else.

693
00:47:34.631 --> 00:47:37.350
The portrait in your room depicts you

694
00:47:37.434 --> 00:47:39.468
alongside Lord Thomas Hamilton.

695
00:47:39.519 --> 00:47:41.971
son of Alfred Hamilton.

696
00:47:42.022 --> 00:47:44.991
the lord proprietor of
these Bahama Islands.

697
00:47:46.476 --> 00:47:48.194
Forgive me.

698
00:47:48.278 --> 00:47:51.280
I must have gotten
disoriented and wandered.

699
00:47:53.917 --> 00:47:56.919
You see. I've had extensive dealings
with the earl over the years.

700
00:47:56.987 --> 00:48:00.623
and so I'd long heard of the tragedy

701
00:48:00.674 --> 00:48:03.426
that befell his eldest son.

702
00:48:03.493 --> 00:48:05.661
<i>But Thomas's wife.</i>

703
00:48:05.712 --> 00:48:08.848
long rumored to be the cheating sort.

704
00:48:08.932 --> 00:48:10.883
had begun a torrid affair

705
00:48:10.968 --> 00:48:13.386
with her husband's closest friend.

706
00:48:13.470 --> 00:48:17.390
a promising young officer
in His Majesty's Navy.

707
00:48:20.110 --> 00:48:22.979
And upon discovering the affair.

708
00:48:23.030 --> 00:48:25.698
Thomas went mad with grief.

709
00:48:27.517 --> 00:48:29.568
<i>His despair so great.</i>

710
00:48:29.653 --> 00:48:32.705
<i>even the asylum couldn't
protect him from himself.</i>

711
00:48:36.827 --> 00:48:38.995
As for Thomas's wife.

712
00:48:39.046 --> 00:48:42.498
she's said to have fled
London along with her lover.

713
00:48:42.549 --> 00:48:45.551
Partly out of shame.

714
00:48:45.635 --> 00:48:48.838
<i>partly to escape retribution.</i>

715
00:48:48.889 --> 00:48:51.474
Given the facts at hand.
I am forced to assume

716
00:48:51.541 --> 00:48:53.759
that the lover is none other

717
00:48:53.844 --> 00:48:56.479
than our friend Captain Flint.

718
00:48:57.781 --> 00:49:00.716
<i>Please understand. I raise this issue</i>

719
00:49:00.767 --> 00:49:03.402
<i>not to disturb or harass you.</i>

720
00:49:03.487 --> 00:49:07.273
In fact. I wish to help you.

721
00:49:09.443 --> 00:49:10.993
Help me?

722
00:49:11.061 --> 00:49:14.663
I can only assume that
your exile in this place

723
00:49:14.731 --> 00:49:17.616
has been less than ideal.

724
00:49:19.402 --> 00:49:22.004
I understand how desperation

725
00:49:22.072 --> 00:49:23.923
may have driven you here.

726
00:49:24.007 --> 00:49:28.044
but perhaps it's time
you were offered a hand

727
00:49:28.095 --> 00:49:30.262
and a return to civilization.

728
00:49:34.351 --> 00:49:36.769
And you could offer me that?

729
00:49:38.855 --> 00:49:43.275
Boston is quite a different
animal from London.

730
00:49:46.613 --> 00:49:48.781
More forgiving of one's past

731
00:49:48.865 --> 00:49:50.733
in a general sense.

732
00:49:50.784 --> 00:49:52.768
And in this specific sense.

733
00:49:52.819 --> 00:49:55.538
with my family's assistance.

734
00:49:55.605 --> 00:49:59.492
one might find total absolution there.

735
00:49:59.576 --> 00:50:01.994
<i>New identities.</i>

736
00:50:02.079 --> 00:50:04.964
<i>A clean start. A new life.</i>

737
00:50:05.048 --> 00:50:07.083
I could do that for you.

738
00:50:07.134 --> 00:50:09.585
Why on earth would you?

739
00:50:09.636 --> 00:50:12.638
<i>Because I know what it
is to be judged unfairly.</i>

740
00:50:12.722 --> 00:50:14.673
And because it's just possible that.

741
00:50:14.758 --> 00:50:17.560
while I am uniquely situated

742
00:50:17.627 --> 00:50:20.062
to offer you your freedom.

743
00:50:20.130 --> 00:50:22.932
you may be able to do the same for me.

744
00:50:40.700 --> 00:50:42.418
<i>Eleanor: Hello. Charles.</i>

745
00:50:51.094 --> 00:50:52.995
You've looked better.

746
00:50:53.046 --> 00:50:54.830
Fuck you.

747
00:50:54.881 --> 00:50:57.216
<i>We're alone.</i>

748
00:50:59.169 --> 00:51:02.104
You don't have to pretend with me.

749
00:51:04.441 --> 00:51:07.143
The fuck did I ever do to you?

750
00:51:08.728 --> 00:51:10.813
You made me look weak.

751
00:51:12.065 --> 00:51:15.284
Standing beside you. I was your lesser.

752
00:51:19.206 --> 00:51:20.539
I was a girl.

753
00:51:23.026 --> 00:51:24.410
<i>From the moment you met me.</i>

754
00:51:24.494 --> 00:51:26.662
<i>you must have known I'd
never settle for that.</i>

755
00:51:28.698 --> 00:51:31.033
For being less than.

756
00:51:31.084 --> 00:51:33.052
That's why I loved you.

757
00:51:36.139 --> 00:51:37.840
And you destroyed me.

758
00:51:39.759 --> 00:51:42.044
<i>I exposed you.</i>

759
00:51:42.095 --> 00:51:44.680
The weakness behind the mask.

760
00:51:49.069 --> 00:51:50.986
The fear.

761
00:51:53.723 --> 00:51:57.359
So much I have taken from you.

762
00:51:59.529 --> 00:52:01.197
And yet still...

763
00:52:03.750 --> 00:52:06.368
you know you could take it all back.

764
00:52:08.872 --> 00:52:11.540
You could be strong again.

765
00:52:11.591 --> 00:52:14.210
<i>You could resist me.</i>

766
00:52:16.046 --> 00:52:19.014
You could take this whole
fucking island from me.

767
00:52:22.686 --> 00:52:25.888
You know exactly what it is you need to do.

768
00:52:25.939 --> 00:52:29.608
Where it is you need to go to do it.

769
00:52:31.645 --> 00:52:33.562
(man's voice) If only you
weren't so goddamn afraid.

770
00:52:33.613 --> 00:52:35.764
(gasps)

771
00:52:35.815 --> 00:52:38.284
<i>(dogs barking)</i>

772
00:53:44.100 --> 00:53:45.467
(grunts)

773
00:53:45.518 --> 00:53:48.270
(groaning)

774
00:53:52.275 --> 00:53:54.810
Ain't this a sad sight?

775
00:53:59.899 --> 00:54:03.352
Miss Guthrie should
have just had you killed.

776
00:54:03.403 --> 00:54:05.854
It would have been more merciful.

777
00:54:05.905 --> 00:54:08.824
Now. are you going to
give me back me whore?

778
00:54:12.412 --> 00:54:15.030
Jesus! On my shoe!

779
00:54:15.081 --> 00:54:17.383
<i>Oh. fuck it. Put him out of his misery.</i>

780
00:54:25.258 --> 00:54:26.541
(sizzles)

781
00:54:26.593 --> 00:54:28.227
Oh. for Christ...

782
00:54:34.601 --> 00:54:36.568
(screams)

783
00:54:36.653 --> 00:54:39.355
(screaming)

784
00:54:44.411 --> 00:54:46.829
Wait!

785
00:54:46.896 --> 00:54:48.113
Listen to me!

786
00:54:54.204 --> 00:54:55.704
The whorehouse.

787
00:54:55.755 --> 00:54:58.424
<i>I'll cut you in for half.</i>

788
00:54:58.508 --> 00:55:01.043
We'll be partners.

789
00:55:01.094 --> 00:55:02.577
Please.

790
00:55:02.629 --> 00:55:05.631
(growls)

791
00:55:05.715 --> 00:55:07.099
<i>(gagging)</i>

792
00:55:07.183 --> 00:55:09.601
<i>(cracks)</i>

793
00:55:25.151 --> 00:55:27.403
<i>(door closes)</i>

794
00:55:29.956 --> 00:55:33.125
Do you know who I am. Pastor?

795
00:55:33.209 --> 00:55:35.210
I do.

796
00:55:35.278 --> 00:55:38.747
You're the reason this island
is infested with criminals.

797
00:55:40.133 --> 00:55:43.285
God teaches us not to
cheer when others stumble.

798
00:55:43.336 --> 00:55:46.638
In your case. I may ask His forgiveness.

799
00:55:46.723 --> 00:55:50.125
And what does God say about redemption?

800
00:55:50.176 --> 00:55:53.178
Accept His love and you'll find it.

801
00:55:53.263 --> 00:55:54.680
What if I was prepared to go further?

802
00:55:54.764 --> 00:55:56.348
Further?

803
00:55:56.433 --> 00:55:59.801
Penance for my past sins.

804
00:55:59.853 --> 00:56:03.071
<i>Good works.</i>

805
00:56:03.139 --> 00:56:05.023
<i>And they begin tonight.</i>

806
00:56:05.108 --> 00:56:07.109
Who's there?

807
00:56:07.160 --> 00:56:09.328
Mr. Scott.

808
00:56:09.412 --> 00:56:11.497
What are you doing here?

809
00:56:11.581 --> 00:56:13.532
I thought you might use a hand.

810
00:56:16.002 --> 00:56:18.454
Bastard's finally bringing
in the first of the guns.

811
00:56:20.323 --> 00:56:21.457
Took him long enough.

812
00:56:23.543 --> 00:56:25.627
He takes his cargo seriously.

813
00:56:28.214 --> 00:56:31.550
You look tired. Why don't I take over?

814
00:56:31.634 --> 00:56:34.470
Miss Guthrie told me I was to see
those guns off with my own eyes.

815
00:56:36.523 --> 00:56:38.807
I understand.

816
00:56:38.858 --> 00:56:40.642
(grunts)

817
00:56:48.201 --> 00:56:51.203
<i>Richard: I brought the
fiends to this place.</i>

818
00:56:52.705 --> 00:56:54.656
Encouraged them.

819
00:56:54.707 --> 00:56:56.708
Enriched them.

820
00:56:56.793 --> 00:56:59.161
Empowered them.

821
00:57:00.964 --> 00:57:03.832
It seems as though my penance
ought to be a simple one.

822
00:57:06.469 --> 00:57:08.170
I will see to it

823
00:57:08.221 --> 00:57:10.255
that they are cast out of this place.

824
00:57:11.558 --> 00:57:13.725
Soon.

825
00:57:13.810 --> 00:57:15.811
And for good.

826
00:57:19.849 --> 00:57:21.733
The Andromache. It can't be.

827
00:57:21.818 --> 00:57:23.318
Captain Bryson hasn't had time to unload.

828
00:57:23.386 --> 00:57:25.320
He didn't. She's riding low.

829
00:57:25.388 --> 00:57:27.689
<i>Those guns are still on board.</i>

830
00:57:27.740 --> 00:57:29.107
<i>Eleanor: What are we going to do?</i>

831
00:57:32.362 --> 00:57:34.363
Get them back.

832
00:57:39.402 --> 00:57:41.770
<i>(theme music playing)</i>

833
